<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72162" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄθομαι</span></b> , only pres. and
		impf., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>take heed,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i>, and always with neg.: abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἀλεγίζει οὐδ᾽ ὄθεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.107
				</span></i>
			 : c. inf., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ὄθεται
				φίλον ἦτορ ἶσον ἐμοὶ φάσθαι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				166
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				182
			</span></i> : with part. for inf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὃς οὐκ ὄθετ᾽ αἴσυλα ῥέζων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					5.403
				</span></i>
			 : c. gen. pers., <i>regard,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σέθεν . . οὐκ ἀλεγίζω, οὐδ᾽ ὄθομαι
					κοτέοντος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.181
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμεῖο οὐκ ὄθεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					3.94
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1.1267
			</span></i>. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀθεύει, ὀθέω,
			ὄθη.</span>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
